<title>USA: FGIC qualifies seven bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies seven bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>FGIC said Tuesday it qualified seven bond issues for insurance slated for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--North Andover, Mass., $12.3 million GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Wylie, Texas $2.7 million of GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Spotsylvania County, Va., $22.2 million GO school bonds.</p>
<p>--Hill County, Mont., $4.3 million of GO bonds.</p>
<p>--Travis County, Texas, $2.9 million of unlimited tax bonds and $6.5 million of certificates of participation.</p>
<p>--Port Allegany School District, Pa., $5 million of GO bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
